  "boundaries": [
    "Four accepted current-revision original skill16 runtime scenarios. Any failed attempts are retained separately and are never promoted to acceptance. Earlier R27 three pre-cast timeouts and its older1080 acceptance remain historical records.",
    "The successful cast applies native confusion state1 and leaves movement at its actual pre-cast value. SPE/result/report retirement is accepted; natural status release, its duration and movement recalculation after release were not tested.",
    "HD replaces only the authenticated64x64 movie window; every native160x96 and physical pixel outside the HD window is checked independently. HD artwork identity/draw operations and three source-neighborhood readbacks are checked; this does not claim all resampled artwork pixels equal a reference.",
    "Classic and missing scenarios accept actual full physical LCD fallback and have hdAccepted:false. Report acknowledgements above are measured from each own real run; natural timeout is allowed without inventing Enter.",
    "All verified historical owned process identities were absent at stored root samples; user8080 PID, creation time and HTTP200 were preserved. Private browser profiles remain retained and excluded.",
    "Hidden-map counters cover18 specified Canvas methods under the real HD battle marker; they are not FPS, mobile, actual resize, visibility or LIUYAN timeout-cause tests.",
    "Failed draft component and terminal-reader checks, including the preserved old-PowerShell JSON-decoding failure, remain tool provenance, not actual game failures. Raw physical CRLF hashes and Git-normalized LF hashes are separate domains. This limited evidence archive is not a portable browser replay."
  ]
